          "Missing 3rd-person form: 'a triangle' is 'it' — 'has', not 'have'.",
          "Wrong tense: this is always true now — present simple 'has', not past 'had'."
        ],
        "explain": "A fact that's always true — present simple; 'have' becomes 'has' with 'it'."
