          "does",
          "do",
          "doing"
        ],
        "correct": 1,
        "wrongReasons": [
          "Wrong tense: 'on Fridays' is a routine, not something happening now.",
          "",
          "Missing -es: with 'my mum' (she), 'do' becomes 'does'.",
          "An -ing form like 'doing' can't be the verb on its own — here you need 'does'."
        ],
        "explain": "'On Fridays' signals a routine — present simple; with 'she', 'do' becomes 'does'."
